Um, but, yeah, the, and you still feel like you don't really know what to go, what to do, where to go.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.500
Um, I don't know if maybe you agree with that, Joe, but.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:35.960
Oh, absolutely. Yeah.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.200
I mean, I, I think that that's, that's exact.

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.980
I mean, I think that you're kind of hitting exactly my thoughts.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:57.340
It's, it's got a great sense of speed and action going on throughout the game, and I think if you are the person who just kind of takes off running and, and doing these large diagonal jumps, the first thing you'll notice is that it's weird that enemies can spawn literally anywhere, including out of the sky.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:02.080
But they also spawn diagonally, so it's not, like, convenient either.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:06.380
They're just, they're, they're coming from nowhere, and they're going in odd directions.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:24.200
So, you're dealing with that, but then if you just kept running and jumping, treating it like, say, a, a, a, a platforming style game, you don't really, like, take the time to understand the layout or explore for, to find the mystic gates or to know, like, what's going on.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:34.200
You're just dodging enemies and not sure, like, if them spawning is, like, in Legend of Kage, you had to kill, like, X amount of enemies to move on.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:39.760
That was, that was their, uh, stage sequence thing, was like, can't move on to the next stage until you kill 10, right?

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:48.160
In this game, they, they've changed that to try to, you know, update it a little bit or at least, um, not make it so repetitive as just kill X number of enemies.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:18:01.820
But I, I actually think the whole, like, the, the speed at which the game wants you to play and the way in which enemies spawn doesn't really encourage this kind of, like, exploration thing that they might have been going for.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:05.560
Yeah, like, I'm blown by half the platforms.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.580
And, like, when I started and I'm like, oh, I guess I should be kind of methodical.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:18.020
But then just the, the foundational controls, it just make you not do that.

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:26.980
Like, between the momentum that you get when you keep moving in one direction, like, it just makes you not really care about what's right in front of you.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:29.100
It makes you just want to keep moving.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:37.660
And so, yeah, if you're trying to explore and find a key, um, that's not really how they should have gone about it.

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:42.260
Yeah. And I think that, like, overall, definitely, you know, definitely a negative thing, obviously.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:49.580
But I think that, like, I, I, I don't know if you guys agree, but, like, I don't want to understate how much I think that they, they kind of nailed the movement.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:51.840
Oh, yeah. They just put it in the wrong game.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:19:10.620
Like, it does feel good, like, that you, you get that, like, anime, like, samurai or whatever, like, sort of, like, warrior that you're trying to go with where it's like, oh, you're, you're kind of, like, almost soaring through the levels because you're so agile and nimble and swift.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.540
And you're kind of, like, just swiping down enemies as you go.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:14.620
Like, you feel awesome.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:16.020
You feel cool.

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:22.800
It just gets really boring really fast because there's no game built around it once you realize that the enemies are really not, never going to present, like, more of a challenge.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:28.240
Even bosses kind of don't really, like, fit into that gameplay style.

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:38.740
But, like, I mean, not to, you know, not to, like, jump ahead to, like, my overall thoughts, but I, I felt, like, because of that, like, I felt kind of like I was playing a tech demo for movement.

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:40.780
Yeah, I mean, like, it felt like.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:59.720
This is the game that it should have been, like, kill X number of enemies, but also maybe it should have been making, like, points matter and almost, just because of how fluid everything is, almost like Devil May Cry-like and, like, you get, like, combos and, like, score adjustments that way.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:07.680
Like, that's how, like, a game that is, like, that moves like this, I feel like it should have been structured.

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:13.140
I know that that doesn't mean anything to anyone, but, yeah, I agree.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:18.920
It seems like they applied some mismatched design elements here.

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:32.620
This game has the opposite problem of modern Sonic games, where modern Sonic games are all about, like, we want to make sure we can make him go fast, but you can still control him in these larger 3D open worlds.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:42.300
And so either he's not feeling fast at all because the worlds are way too large, or he's moving so fast that you're missing out on everything that's happening.

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:46.240
You know, all the stuff that they poured into the game, you're just completing it in two minutes.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:21:04.480
It's this game has the opposite problem because it's, like, there's a whole, the game actually probably wants you to play a little bit slower, but they designed their character to just, to just do, to go way too fast and for enemies to spawn way too rapidly that you can't kind of, like, just, you know, not stroll around, but you can't even, like, take in what's going on.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:08.260
You're just constantly fighting off enemies and figuring out, like, is this where I need to be?

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:09.660
No. Okay. Is this where I need to be?

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.420
No. Okay. And just keep moving and moving.

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:13.060
Mm-hmm. Yeah.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:15.840
And you can normally just bypass anything that's in your way.

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:19.060
Like, there's no, there's no platforming obstacles.

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:21.080
You can just jump so high, you just get past it.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:24.640
And enemies, I mean, you kill most of them in one hit, or you can just jump past them.

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:28.040
There's really no, there's no reason to not just rush to the boss.

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.420
Yeah, I mean, you gotta get a key, but otherwise, like.

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:32.300
Well, what's up with the bosses, too?

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:37.660
Because, you know, I didn't get to the end of the game, but, like, some of these bosses, only two hits, and they're done?

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:41.760
I don't remember a situation killing them in two hits.

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:45.960
Maybe you. Yeah, I don't either.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:52.060
I remember situations where you can just kind of lock them and hit them a dozen times, and then they die, but they won't hit back.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:53.880
But, yeah, I didn't remember any two hitters.

00:21:53.940 --> 00:21:55.400
Well, were you guys using the magic?

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:58.140
Oh, it took me a while to learn how to use it, yeah.

00:21:58.140 --> 00:21:59.660
Almost never. Right, right.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:02.620
Right. Well, you would just use the magic for the bosses.

00:22:02.660 --> 00:22:11.980
I would actually argue that, you know, for the rest of the enemies, the ones that are just one-hit KOs, no reason to use the magic, because if you miss, it's no different than missing with your sword, right?

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:18.820
Yeah.

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:24.300
So, like, why bother?

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:27.280
But I guess I was doing it wrong still.

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:31.460
But did anyone else also feel like the bosses had almost no AI?

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:37.180
Like, it was like they were just programmed to just swipe, just swing and walk around and hope that you get in their way?

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:40.040
Well, I thought it was canon that all the enemies are blind.

00:22:41.140 --> 00:22:42.140
Oh, was that canon?

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:45.900
Yeah. I thought that was canon that, like, this army of demons can't see.

00:22:46.540 --> 00:22:56.340
Yeah. And I noticed there's, like, I think it's the second boss where it's more of, like, a wizard than it is a swordsman.

00:22:56.340 --> 00:23:06.440
And it will, it has some kind of AI where it will do its best to avoid you so it can use, like, a ranged attack, I think.

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:11.140
But other than that, yeah, they just, they don't really have a pattern.

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:18.580
They're just larger, more HP-heavy versions of the goofballs that are flying at you in the woods.

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:27.380
Yeah, and because they have that, I don't even know if this is the correct term or not, but in a lot of RPGs lately, it's been used as, like, staggering the enemy.

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:33.620
Mm-hmm. Where, you know, because it has that effect on the bosses, too, they're not that challenging.

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:44.180
If you get them in, like, that sweet spot where you can kind of, like, attack them and then they're, like, stuck in, like, a state of animation where they look like they're taking damage, but then they can continue to take damage.

00:23:44.760 --> 00:23:47.160
You know, I'm not sure why they would design it like that.

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:51.780
It should be more like you hit them and then they have a small period of invincibility or something.

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:57.300
If they want it to be a more methodical, like, battle situation.

00:23:57.460 --> 00:23:58.420
Right, right. Yeah.

00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:07.180
But we're not even playing the real game, so what's the point, right, of talking about Demon Sword here?

00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:09.280
Because Japan got the real game.

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:22.080
On the Famicom, there are six more stages, several more bosses, more items, more magic spells, and the ending in the Japanese version has extra scenes that weren't included.

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:30.500
Oh. They cut a lot of text and basically just ended the NES version, but in Japan it actually, like, has more of a story to it.

00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:32.900
So we did just get a tech demo.

00:24:33.300 --> 00:24:34.740
Well, didn't you feel that was weird at the end?

00:24:34.780 --> 00:24:35.940
I mean, I don't know if you guys saw the end.

00:24:36.020 --> 00:24:46.020
I watched it on YouTube. It's just him riding a horse in the desert and then, like, the time just changes, but there's no text explaining what's happening.

00:24:46.040 --> 00:24:48.220
You're just watching him ride a horse.

00:24:49.200 --> 00:24:50.500
No, I did see it.

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:54.300
So they remove the story from the game.

00:24:54.740 --> 00:25:02.000
I mean, I thought, okay, so you throw your completed Demon Sword into the head of a demon, and I'm like, okay, I did it.

00:25:02.080 --> 00:25:07.940
I thought that was just you, like, on your farewell tour going back, you know, to work at Applebee's or something.

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:09.140
And then they just did it.

00:25:09.160 --> 00:25:10.360
Yeah, but they could have put that as text.

00:25:10.520 --> 00:25:14.060
They could have been like, yeah, and then Vitar went back to Applebee's.

00:25:14.840 --> 00:25:16.000
That's true. They could have done that.

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:17.960
Or the Wizarding World of Harry Potter.

00:25:19.220 --> 00:25:21.520
And he goes to, like, a portal into another planet.

00:25:24.060 --> 00:25:25.780
Wow. Because that's how it works.

00:25:26.080 --> 00:25:27.060
That's all the...

00:25:27.060 --> 00:25:28.140
Oh, God.

00:25:28.600 --> 00:25:32.340
I couldn't think of the word for callbacks, but it's all of them right there.

00:25:32.420 --> 00:25:34.540
That's the word, yeah. You actually did think of it.

00:25:34.660 --> 00:25:39.040
Mm-hmm. I just love how on this screen all the stars are just in clusters of three.

00:25:39.180 --> 00:25:41.460
It's just like a bunch of Orion's belts in the sky.

00:25:41.740 --> 00:25:44.100
Hey, man. That's all stars are.

00:25:48.900 --> 00:25:50.140
What else you got, Mike?

00:25:50.260 --> 00:25:56.600
What do we got? I was just checking the Demon Sword Famicom play, but I guess it's called something different,

00:25:56.620 --> 00:25:58.600
so it's really hard for me to find it.

00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:00.400
Sorry about that.

00:26:00.780 --> 00:26:05.080
Like, thought I'd have a good answer for what happens next.

00:26:05.280 --> 00:26:09.860
But basically, from what I can see, yeah, he reunites with his...

00:26:09.860 --> 00:26:13.480
Oh, you know what? Actually, the horse thing is supposed to be silent.

00:26:13.480 --> 00:26:17.680
So at least they didn't jip us of, like, some contextual things there.

00:26:17.840 --> 00:26:18.780
They just...

00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:19.920
Oh, wait a minute.

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:20.800
Now, this is strange.

00:26:20.800 --> 00:26:29.080
Okay, sorry that it's all, like, live react, but the Famicom version has the text after the

00:26:29.080 --> 00:26:32.220
cowboy scene, after he's riding the horse into the desert.

00:26:32.280 --> 00:26:36.820
It has English text to explain what happens next.

00:26:36.820 --> 00:26:38.960
Praise to the great...

00:26:38.960 --> 00:26:41.060
That word looks wrong, but it's like Vajra.

00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:43.320
V-A-J-R-A.

00:26:43.560 --> 00:26:49.960
Vajra. With great wrath, he will violently destroy all obstacles.

00:26:50.200 --> 00:26:51.980
Oh, so Vajra must be Victar.

00:26:52.540 --> 00:26:56.640
Ah. That sounds pretty, like, just destructive.

00:26:57.020 --> 00:27:00.820
Are we sure that Vajra isn't, like, another villain?

00:27:02.160 --> 00:27:03.600
Yeah, it sounds like we got the bad ending.

00:27:03.740 --> 00:27:05.140
Yeah. Right?

00:27:05.260 --> 00:27:06.500
Like, he's gonna destroy...

00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:11.540
With great wrath, he will violently destroy all obstacles.

00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:15.060
Yeah, that sounds like not what a good guy would do.

00:27:15.160 --> 00:27:21.800
He would, like, reluctantly destroy all obstacles because he must, because the prophecy was foretold,

00:27:22.260 --> 00:27:23.620
but... Maybe he's an anti-hero.

00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:26.200
Maybe. Maybe this is the first anti-hero.

00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:29.140
And he doesn't go back to work at Applebee's.

00:27:29.300 --> 00:27:32.520
He goes back to work at, like, Popeye's.

00:27:33.860 --> 00:27:38.000
Is Popeye's, like, the anti-heroes version of Applebee's?

00:27:38.120 --> 00:27:41.920
Well, I guess, you know, anybody that works at Popeye's is, like, they're mean.

00:27:42.300 --> 00:27:47.380
I would have thought TGI Friday's is the, like, anti-hero version of Applebee's.

00:27:47.620 --> 00:27:48.560
Yeah, you're right.

00:27:48.660 --> 00:27:57.040
If you're going by fast cash, sit-down restaurants, then maybe TGI Friday's does fit that bill.

00:27:57.300 --> 00:27:58.420
Was this in the manual?

00:27:58.420 --> 00:28:00.400
Uh, yeah. The one I wrote.

00:28:00.900 --> 00:28:08.760
I'm somewhat understanding of, like, oh, it comes to North America and they made the game harder or they made the game easier, right?

00:28:08.820 --> 00:28:17.060
Like, I can understand some weird executive logic there for why they would make those kinds of decisions based on renting and stuff like that.

00:28:17.060 --> 00:28:23.900
But why cut content, like, like, full stages and bosses and items and magic spells?

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:25.980
Like, what's the point there?

00:28:26.180 --> 00:28:27.400
At what point do you just say, like...

00:28:27.400 --> 00:28:30.880
Yeah, that's... No, that does feel like the freeware version.

00:28:30.880 --> 00:28:33.700
Like, the demo version of an actual game.

00:28:33.860 --> 00:28:35.620
Three of nine levels.

00:28:36.260 --> 00:28:38.360
Like, that's crazy.

00:28:38.840 --> 00:28:41.640
Yeah, and also, I mean, even, like...

00:28:41.640 --> 00:28:47.420
Yeah, I mean, I was going to say the same thing about, like, translation stuff where it's like, okay, maybe they didn't want to translate this and, like, you gotta, I guess, do some recoding.

00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:50.380
But I feel like cutting magic...

00:28:50.380 --> 00:28:52.220
I mean, isn't that extra work?

00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:55.340
Yeah. Don't you have to actually cut the spells out of the game?

00:28:55.360 --> 00:28:56.440
Well, maybe they're in the data.

00:28:56.440 --> 00:29:01.520
Like, why do that? They just don't have any actual program drops for them or something.

00:29:02.280 --> 00:29:05.780
But, like, was there something where it's like, oh, this magic is offensive to Americans?

00:29:06.220 --> 00:29:10.540
Or, like, I know, like, the only other one I could really think of was, like, Casino Kid, where they cut out, like, content like that.

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:12.460
And, like, that, I guess I understood a little bit.

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:17.720
Maybe we were just, like, a little more strict on, like, gambling in a kid's game.

00:29:17.800 --> 00:29:21.160
But this was, like, the magic, like, graphic or something?

00:29:21.340 --> 00:29:30.600
Like, I don't know. Well, we can talk about the Famicom version all we want, but we're only allowed to vote on the North American version in the Essential Games List.

00:29:33.500 --> 00:29:35.100
And I go first on these things.

00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:39.660
Still working on that transition, but we're going to nail it eventually, right, guys?

00:29:40.280 --> 00:29:42.320
We're not going to transition, so.

00:29:43.160 --> 00:29:44.220
Yeah. Mike?

00:29:44.660 --> 00:29:45.540
Thank you. Yeah, yeah.

00:29:45.640 --> 00:29:46.460
Throw it to me. There you go.

00:29:46.640 --> 00:29:50.240
Well, guys, you know, since you asked, no, obviously not.

00:29:50.900 --> 00:29:55.400
We weren't even talking about the game for most of this episode, much to our own amusement, too.

00:29:55.520 --> 00:29:58.640
I had more fun recording this episode with you guys than I had playing with this game.

00:29:58.900 --> 00:30:01.220
It was funny because I didn't know that Demon Sword.

00:30:01.520 --> 00:30:02.880
It was the Legend of Kage folks.

